Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/packet-net/axcall
Description: connected-mode AX.25 terminal over KISS
 Dials a remote AX.25 station, pipes your keyboard to it and its replies to
 your screen, and disconnects cleanly. Line mode, 8 bit clean, transparent
 CR/LF translation.
 .
 Unlike the axcall from ax25-apps, this one does not use the Linux kernel
 AX.25 stack, which has been withdrawn. It carries its own AX.25 v2.2 data
 link and speaks KISS to a TNC over a serial port or over TCP, so it needs no
 kernel support, no kissattach, no axparms and no privilege. The command line
 is deliberately the old one, so existing scripts mostly carry over.
 .
 Self-contained: bundles its own .NET runtime, so no system runtime is
 required. Replaces ax25-apps, which owns the same /usr/bin/axcall; the rest
 of that package (axlisten, ax25ipd, ax25rtd, ax25mond) depends on the
 withdrawn kernel stack and no longer functions.

